        "evidence": "confined-particle.lean:52 `def confined : ConfinedParticle → ℝ → Prop := fun _ _ => True`, with the docstring 'Concrete model: every particle is confined at every q' (lean lines 47-48). The .md (confined-particle.md:33-37) defines confinement as a non-trivial q-indexed predicate that 'holds iff the matrix Frobenius PSD cone admits a feasible Φ* ⪰ 0 (confinement SDP).'",
        "notes": "The Lean `confined` predicate is the constant `True`, so it proves something strictly weaker/vacuous relative to the .md's SDP-feasibility predicate. The Lean comment is honest that it is a surrogate stub, but the named decl `confined` formalizes the .md's central confinement notion as a tautology — proof-statement-integrity divergence. The structures MarkovClass/ConfinedParticle (lean 23-41) do faithfully mirror the tuple, so the tuple part is fine; the divergence is the `confined` predicate specifically. Note: the .ts lean.ref points to QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinedParticle (the structure), not to `confined`, which mitigates but does not remove the in-file stub."
